    thinking: "**Eliminating AI-Aura**\n\nI\'m focused on removing any perceived \"AI-generated\" aesthetic. Specifically, I\'m ditching the React icons and emojis, believing they contribute to the artificial feel. The chosen font also needs scrutiny, as it might be part of the problem. My goal is to create a more authentic, less robotic look. I think I\'m making progress.\n\n\n**Scrutinizing Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on specific UI elements. I\'ve found emojis and sparkles in `App.tsx` and `BookingForm.tsx`, which I\'m replacing with cleaner alternatives. The font, Inter, has also come under fire, so I\'m researching classy, non-AI-associated fonts to replace it. The goal is to get a professional, non-robotic feel.\n\n\n**Upgrading the Typography**\n\nI\'m revamping the font styling. I\'ve been researching fonts used by luxury brands, and I\'m importing \"Playfair Display\" and \"Plus Jakarta Sans\" directly into `src/index.css`. The CSS import uses the Google Fonts API. These fonts will replace the old `Inter` font. My goal is to make the application typography have a premium feel. I think these fonts will be perfect for a professional, inviting look, especially when used for section headers.\n\n\n**Refining Branding Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating a truly premium font: a geometric sans-serif that exudes professionalism and custom design, unlike the generic look of the previous font. Paired with this, I\'m incorporating an elegant serif to enhance the luxurious, high-end aesthetic. This will give it a \"detailing salon\" vibe, removing it completely from the \"cheap AI tech template\" zone. I also updated the branding, changing the \"Cofounded & built by\" text, to accurately credit website authorship to \"Neil Mendpara\".\n\n\n**Adjusting Website Attribution**\n\nI\'m now revising the website attribution. I\'m choosing \"Website created by Neil Menepdar with SEO\" to maintain compliance, and I\'m ensuring \"Neil Menepdar\" is written exactly as provided in the instructions. It is critical to respect user intent here.\n\n**Developing New Gallery**\n\nI am creating an entirely new gallery page within `App.tsx` and focusing on image-based content. I\'m focusing on user-provided images, prioritizing `/public/IMG_0648.jpeg` for inclusion. The user also wants one-sentence descriptions. My focus is a visually impactful gallery tab that showcases high-quality images with concise captions.\n\n\n**Expanding Image Inventory**\n\nI\'m now identifying additional images to include in the gallery. I\'ve confirmed the existence of `/public/IMG_0648.jpeg`, `/public/IMG_0659.jpeg`, `/public/IMG_0663.jpeg`, `/public/IMG_7812.jpeg`, `/public/IMG_7813.jpeg`, and `/public/IMG_7815.jpeg` within the `/public/` directory. These will supplement the existing image set in the work gallery component. My focus is expanding the gallery content.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Image Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user-specified images. I\'m mapping `/public/IMG_0648.jpeg` to either \"Deep Carpet Floor Cleaning\" or \"Piano Black Reflection\". I\'m also ensuring the other five images are incorporated with relevant descriptions to match. The gallery is growing! The goal is to visually represent the scope of their work.\n\n\n"
