  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Aesthetic Choices**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s feedback concerning the site\'s visual elements. Specifically, the reaction icons and overall font aesthetic are under scrutiny. The user suggests they appear artificial, a common trait of AI-generated content. I\'m focusing on making the website feel more human-centered, and less generic. I will remove the word \"cofounded\", change the font and add images.\n\n\n**Refining Page Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the gallery page. I need to showcase the piano black image and floor cleaning visuals, aiming for a clean, impactful presentation. I\'m focusing on concise descriptions and flashy titles to match the images, avoiding excessive pop-ups and long explanations. Typography is updated with Google Fonts. I\'m prioritizing human-centered design principles.\n\n\n**Optimizing Visual Presentation**\n\nI\'m now implementing \"fair Display\" for titles and integrating these fonts into `src/index.css` via the Tailwind `@theme` block. I\'m also setting `font-serif` for main headings and `font-sans` elsewhere, with deep black and warm amber tones, generous negative space, and sophisticated layout padding to achieve a luxurious feel.\n\n**Boosting SEO Visibility**\n\nI\'m focusing now on SEO, adding rich meta tags and OpenGraph data to `index.html`, including geo-tags for Cobb County and surrounding areas. I will ensure headings are logically structured with HTML tags containing high-value local search keywords for detailing services.\n\n\n**Clarifying Pricing Details**\n\nI\'m now revising price indicators and booking estimates across the site. I\'m swapping \"transparent pricing\" with \"Estimate (Subject to size/condition)\" in `src/App.tsx`. I\'ll update the pricing with starting prices or variable ranges. In `src/components/ServicesDetail.tsx`, I\'ll add clarifying notes. Finally, the booking form will receive size/condition considerations.\n\n\n**Revising User Interface**\n\nI am currently working on making the user interface feel more genuine and less AI-generated. I\'m removing the React icons and emojis the user found objectionable, replacing them with more understated alternatives. Also, I\'ve altered the website\'s attribution line in `src/App.tsx`, replacing \"Cofounded & built by\" with \"Website created by Neil Menepdar with SEO\" to simplify the statement. I also want to make sure the site doesn\'t give a generic look.\n\n\n**Simplifying Booking Process**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the booking form in `/src/components/BookingForm.tsx`, focusing solely on vehicle type instead of make, model, and year. I\'ve updated the prompt to \"Vehicle Type *\" and adjusted the validation message for clarity. I will add a new gallery tab to match the \"PIANO BLACK IMAGE\", named \"Work Gallery\", using the `WorkGallery` component, no pop-ups, 1-sentence descriptions. The tab will align with other navigation options: Overview, Services, Request Spot.\n\n\n**Showcasing Work Visually**\n\nI\'m developing a new visual showroom, the \"Work Gallery,\" to feature our best work. This gallery in `src/components/WorkGallery.tsx` will present images with flashy titles and concise descriptions, ensuring an impactful and easy-to-browse experience. The visual layout, with geometric cards, will showcase the quality of our services. The gallery is replacing \"detailed popups\".\n\n\n**Labeling Image Content**\n\nI\'m now identifying and labeling images for the \"Work Gallery\" with descriptive, high-value detailing terms. I\'ve matched each image path to a descriptive title and concise description: \"/public/IMG_0648.jpeg\" is \"Deep Floor Carpet & Fibers Extraction\"; \"/public/IMG_7813.jpeg\" is \"Mirror-Shine Piano Black Trim Restoration\"; \"/public/IMG_0663.jpeg\" is \"Crystalline Cockpit Glass & Dashboard Conditioning\"; \"/public/IMG_7812.jpeg\" is \"Flawless Clear Coat Refraction\"; and \"/public/IMG_7815.jpeg\" is \"Precision Rim & Brake Caliper Care.\"\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will update the global CSS file `src/index.css` to load two premium Google Fonts: **Playfair Display** (for elite display-worthy headings) and **Plus Jakarta Sans** (a clean, modern, architectural geometric sans-serif for general UI and reading list items). This instantly replaces the \"generic, automated layout font\" look with a custom-designed aesthetic."
