  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining the Gallery Build**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with the current WorkGallery component; it\'s beautifully set up. All required `/public/IMG_xxxx.jpeg` images are structured dynamically. It showcases \"PIANO BLACK\" and \"FLOOR CLEANING EVERYTHING GOTTA BE NICE AND SHOWCASED\" without any bloated popup modals or zooming overlays, and works smoothly. It is Flash free too!\n\n\n**Adjusting the Booking Form**\n\nI\'m now focusing on `src/components/BookingForm.tsx`. I\'ve successfully imported `motion/react` and will use `<motion.div>` for animations. The \"Vehicle Year, Make & Model\" label is changed to \"Vehicle Type,\" and the placeholder is updated to better reflect examples. I must also remember to clarify that all prices are not necessarily set, and do depend on size and dirtiness.\n\n\n**Clarifying Service Pricing**\n\nI\'m now implementing updates to the `BookingForm.tsx` component. Specifically, I\'m working to make the service pricing clearer. I\'m adding clarifying text and asterisks near the service packages and their respective prices to emphasize that they are starting estimates. I have reviewed the render section and specific lines for the labels, price displays, and submit actions, in order to make edits. I\'m looking to add text to convey that the ultimate price depends on vehicle size and dirtiness.\n\n\n**Revising Success Animation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the success animation within the `BookingForm.tsx` component. I\'m focusing on lines 138-180 and have decided to wrap the entire form and success panels in an `<AnimatePresence>` block. This replaces the conditional rendering based on `bookingRef`. Inside `<AnimatePresence>`, the success message will be a `<motion.div>` with `initial`, `animate`, and `exit` properties to achieve a smooth crossfade animation when `bookingRef` transitions.\n\n\n**Implementing Form Animations**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating Framer Motion into the `BookingForm.tsx` component to create smooth transitions. I\'ve wrapped the form and success panels in `<AnimatePresence>` for seamless crossfading, replacing the conditional rendering with `<motion.div>`. I\'m now adding error message animations, using `initial`, `animate`, and `exit` properties. This should fulfill both animation tasks!\n\n\n**Adding Error Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating error message animation with Framer Motion in `BookingForm.tsx`. I have the design and logic sorted, and I\'m focusing on the error message visual indicators. I\'m adding a specific alert triangle icon and styling to visually emphasize error messages to the user. I\'m looking into the submit button\'s disabled state, and the loader animation too.\n\nI also see a Sparkles icon to add to the submit button, so I will now add that.\n\n\n**Refining Button Aesthetics**\n\nI\'ve just had a major aesthetic correction: I am removing all \"sparkles\" and flashy AI-generated icons from the submit button and throughout `BookingForm.tsx`. I\'ll replace the `<Sparkles>` icon with a clean chevron or arrow or simply bold text for \"Reserve Driveway Booking\" for a premium and authentic look. I must now review lines 236-248 in `BookingForm.tsx`.\n\n\n**Updating Vehicle Type Input**\n\nI\'m now revising the vehicle type input field within the `BookingForm.tsx` component. I\'ve updated the label from \"Vehicle Year, Make & Model\" to \"Vehicle Type,\" and refined the placeholder text. I\'ve also incorporated the `required` attribute. Furthermore, I\'ve updated the validation check to reflect the new field.\n\n\n**Clarifying Pricing Estimates**\n\nI\'m now revising the `BookingForm.tsx` to clarify service pricing estimates. I\'m adding \"Est. Starting at\" to the price display, and including an explanatory note about the price variability based on vehicle size and dirtiness, just below the label. I\'m checking the pricing display and overall layout to make sure everything\'s correct.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now update `src/components/BookingForm.tsx` to:\n1. **Import `motion` and `AnimatePresence`** from `\"motion/react\"` to cleanly animate transitions for success banners and error states.\n2. **Remove Sparkles icons** and references to prevent any cheap \"AI-generated boilerplate\" styling.\n3. **Simplify the vehicle input field** to ask for `\"Vehicle Type *\"` (SUV, Sedan, Truck, etc.) rather than Year, Make, and Model.\n4. **Make the pricing estimate-based**: add prominent, professional notices stating that pricing represents starting estimates which depend directly on vehicle size and condition/dirtiness."
